cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived version used in your work."
type: software
title: "Climate NetCDF aggregation tools"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Hongren
    affiliation: University of Waterloo
repository-code: "https://github.com/hongren-shen/climate-netcdf-aggregation"
url: "https://github.com/hongren-shen/climate-netcdf-aggregation"
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Python tools for area-weighted aggregation of prepared gridded NetCDF
  meteorological forcing to gauge basins, subbasins, and hydrologic response
  units. The tools write aggregated NetCDF files, Raven grid weights, and text
  metadata files. Optional steps include temporal aggregation, daily temperature
  statistics, and ZIP creation. The example uses CaSR v3.1 forcing and OWL-Hydro
  routing products for gauge 02KA015 in southeastern Ontario, with the SE 24H
  gauge inventory. The forcing covers 2020 and includes a buffer of five grid
  cells around the gauge basin.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - meteorological forcing
  - NetCDF
  - spatial aggregation
  - temporal aggregation
  - CaSR
  - OWL-Hydro
  - Raven
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Grid Weights Generator for Raven"
    authors:
      - family-names: Mai
        given-names: Juliane
    repository-code: "https://github.com/julemai/GridWeightsGenerator"
    url: "https://github.com/julemai/GridWeightsGenerator"
